(Citations and Verification) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A citation is only useful if the reader can act on it. That means every) Tj T*
(chunk must carry the file it came from and its position within that) Tj T*
(file: a page number for a PDF, a section heading for a text document.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Citations should be derived from the chunks that were actually sent to) Tj T*
(the model, not by parsing markers out of the generated prose. A model) Tj T*
(that invents a bracket number has not invented a source; it has) Tj T*
(invented a reference to a source that was present. Letting the) Tj T*
(prose drive the citation list makes that failure visible to the user.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Showing the retrieved text itself, alongside the answer, is what makes) Tj T*
(a grounded system auditable. A reader can check whether the cited) Tj T*
(passage really supports the claim in one glance.) Tj T*
